# Line-ending discipline for byte-hashed files (S110).
#
# The refine gold vault (agents/refine_gold_s105/) is byte-frozen with a sha256 manifest, and
# verify_gold.py additionally byte-compares the LIVE agent reasoning files against their gold twins.
# On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, git rewrites these files to CRLF and every hash
# "mismatches" - a false TAMPERED verdict that hard-blocks all forecast runs (hit in S110).
# Pin them to the committed LF bytes on every platform so the vault hash is checkout-invariant.
research/kalshi/agents/refine_gold_s105/** -text
research/kalshi/agents/*.md text eol=lf

# Granite prompt fixtures are byte-frozen (sha256 asserted by tests/test_granite_contract.py);
# the same autocrlf rewrite would break them on a Windows checkout.
research/kalshi/frankie_boss/tests/fixtures/granite_prompts/** -text

# Exact official cancellation schema reference is checked at runtime.
research/kalshi/frankie_boss/provenance/kalshi-cancel-order-v2-20260915.md -text

# Byte-exact Sunday working-tree captures: mixed CRLF/LF bytes that git normalisation would destroy
research/kalshi/frankie_boss/sunday_20260915_package/FB/sunday-launch-20260915/Markets/** -text
